diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 755246d..b9a036c 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -140,3 +140,80 @@ We indicate externally borrowed code and model components here:
 
 - Beta fitting is adapted from [joint2smpl](https://github.com/wangsen1312/joints2smpl) and [VIBE](https://github.com/mkocabas/VIBE).
 - The SMPL-X body model and layer are provided by [SMPL-X](https://github.com/vchoutas/smplx).
+
+## Joint shape + hand fitting (`--fit-shape-hands`)
+
+SMPL-X has no separate hand shape space; hands share the body `shapedirs`.
+`--fit-shape-hands` replaces the first-frame, body-only beta fit with a joint
+optimisation of `--num-betas` shape coefficients (default 16) together with
+body and finger poses on `--shape-frames` frames spread over the clip (default
+8). Targets are the 22 body joints, the 30 HiPHI finger joints and the 10
+fingertip End Sites, so the fitted shape also respects hand proportions. It
+needs no SMPLify resources.
+
+```bash
+hiphi2smplx --input-bvh motion_actor.bvh --output motion_smplx.npz \
+  --model-path assets/models/SMPLX_NEUTRAL.npz \
+  --fit-shape-hands --num-betas 16 --beta-device cuda:0
+```
+
+The saved `betas` then has `--num-betas` entries.
+
+## Hand IK (`--fit-hands`)
+
+`--fit-hands` solves both wrists and all 30 finger joints right after the body
+IK with the same sequential Mink differential-IK approach (one 16-ball-joint
+chain per hand, warm-started from the previous frame). Targets are the HiPHI
+finger joints and fingertip End Sites: their bone *directions* are combined
+with the shaped SMPL-X bone lengths, and finger segments are chained from the
+current metacarpal ends, so the rigid SMPL-X palm never fights the BVH palm.
+Typical result: about 4 degrees mean bone-direction error, with the same
+temporal smoothness as the body IK; roughly 5 ms per frame for both hands.
+
+```bash
+hiphi2smplx --input-bvh motion_actor.bvh --output motion_smplx.npz \
+  --model-path assets/models/SMPLX_NEUTRAL.npz \
+  --fit-shape-hands --fit-hands --beta-device cuda:0
+```
+
+## Stage 2: HOI refinement (`hiphi2smplx-hoi`)
+
+`hiphi2smplx-hoi` refines a stage-1 result (body IK + `--fit-hands`) against
+the tracked object of a HiPHI HOI package. The correction is a *low-frequency*
+cubic B-spline in time (knots every `--basis-spacing` frames, default 9 =
+10 Hz) added to every stage-1 parameter, so it cannot introduce frame-to-frame
+jitter; all frames share one coefficient set optimised with Adam (cosine LR
+decay). Terms, on a libigl fast-winding-number SDF of the object mesh:
+
+- **penetration penalty**: SDF hinge with a 0.5 cm margin plus a normal-guided
+  term that pushes penetrating vertices back along their own body normal
+  (needed for thin chair seats and table tops);
+- **contact attraction**: BVH fingertips within 2 cm of the object (flags
+  majority-filtered in time) pull the distal-phalanx vertices onto the surface;
+  body vertices within a 2 cm band are attracted to the surface;
+- **anchors**: body joints to the stage-1 joints (`--w-joint-anchor`), finger
+  rotations to the stage-1 fingers (`--w-hand-prior`), plus the BVH finger
+  direction term.
+
+```bash
+hiphi2smplx-hoi \
+  --package /path/to/HiPHI/data/{frame}/{lu}/{motion_id} \
+  --stage1 /path/to/motion_smplx.npz \
+  --output /path/to/motion_smplx_hoi.npz \
+  --stats /path/to/motion_smplx_hoi.json \
+  --model-path assets/models/SMPLX_NEUTRAL.npz \
+  --repo-root /path/to/HiPHI --sdf-cache /path/to/sdf_cache \
+  --basis-spacing 9 --iters-full 120 --w-joint-anchor 0.3
+```
+
+The output keeps the AMASS-style layout and adds `tip_contact` with shape
+`(frames, 10)`: BVH-derived contact flags for left thumb..pinky, right
+thumb..pinky. The stats JSON reports penetration depth, frames penetrating
+more than 1 cm, fingertip-to-object distance on contact frames, hand bone
+direction error and joint acceleration (jitter), each before and after.
+Typical effect on HiPHI: frames penetrating >1 cm drop by 85 to 99 percent
+for boxes, tables and chair manipulation, fingertip contact distance drops to
+0.2 to 0.4 cm, and joint acceleration stays within 0.05 mm/frame^2 of stage 1.
+Seated motions are the exception: SMPL-X thighs are thicker than the actors',
+so removing seat penetration requires lifting the body several centimetres
+above the BVH joints, and the default anchor only partially does so.
